{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_apple_design", "label": "Apple Fluid Interfaces Design (WWDC)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_interruptibility", "label": "Interruptibility Principle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": "3. Interruptibility", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The thought and the gesture happen in parallel: every animation must be grabbable and redirectable mid-flight, always animating from the presentation (current on-screen) value never the target, because starting from the logical value causes a visible jump. Springs are the tool because they are inherently interruptible and velocity-aware."}, {"id": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_momentum_projection", "label": "Momentum Projection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": "6. Momentum projection", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Project the resting position from release velocity via exponential decay (v/1000 * d/(1-d), d~0.998) and snap to the nearest target of the projection, not the release point; the physics-textbook v^2/(2*decel) is deliberately not what Apple ships."}, {"id": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_spring_parameters", "label": "Damping Ratio + Response Spring Parameters", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": "4. Behavior over animation", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Apple deliberately replaced the mass/stiffness/damping physics triplet with two designer-friendly parameters (damping ratio for overshoot, response for speed); default to damping 1.0 everywhere and add bounce ~0.8 only when the gesture itself carried momentum."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_apple_design", "target": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_interruptibility", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_apple_design", "target": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_momentum_projection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_apple_design", "target": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_spring_parameters", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_spring_parameters", "target": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_design_design_guide", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": "Web mapping (Motion / Framer Motion)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_spring_parameters", "target": "_claude_skills_motion_css_spring_index_css_spring_generation", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": ".claude/skills/design-engineering/apple.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_apple_interruptibility", "target": "_claude_skills_design_engineering_design_sonner_principles", "relation": "sem